
== §1 — NO FIRE DESIGN, NO SIMULATION, NO CODE ==
  ✓ the FLS spec implements no fire code value
  ✓ the spec states in writing that there is no Fire / Life-Safety engine
  ✓ the only mentions of a fire code are in the forbidden lists and the denial text
  ✓ regulatory rule count is still zero
  ✓ real occupancy classification count is still zero
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_fls.json
  ✓ twelve FLS element types declared
  ✓ twenty-two device types declared
  ✓ COMPLIANT / SAFE / APPROVED / CERTIFIED / DESIGNED are not model statuses
  ✓ UNSAFE / CODE_VIOLATION / FIRE_VIOLATION are not severities
  ✓ no compiled FLS element carries a coverage, hydraulic or compliance field
  ✓ no invented K-factor, density, candela, audibility or travel limit appears in any field
  ✓ the language actually used is representational

== §2 — CODE_REQUIRED GATE ==
  ✓ code_required and rule are not provenance values
  ✓ they are named explicitly as forbidden provenance
  ✓ a model claiming code_required provenance is neutralised, not obeyed
  ✓ every audit reports code_required as exactly zero
  ✓ a system-added Phase 1 smoke detector stays system_default through two adapters
  ✓ a user-supplied Phase 1 point keeps its user provenance
  ✓ the string code_required does not appear in the compiled models at all

== §3 — ADAPTERS DO NOT DUPLICATE ==
  ✓ exits come from the egress foundation, not a second inference engine
  ✓ an adapted exit references the egress exit id
  ✓ the FLS exit list matches the egress exit list exactly
  ✓ stairs are referenced from the architectural cores
  ✓ an adapted stair creates no geometry, only a reference
  ✓ the render layer marks referenced devices as referenced, not emitted
  ✓ an FLS-declared device IS emitted, because nothing else draws it
  ✓ the spec states the no-duplication rule in writing
  ✓ MEP fire systems are referenced, not re-modelled
  ✓ the MEP model stays the source of truth for topology
  ✓ no FLS element maintains a sprinkler pipe network

== §4 — DEVICE PRESENT IS NOT COVERAGE ==
  ✓ one declared detector yields exactly one represented device
  ✓ the audit reports coverage and compliance as NOT_EVALUATED
  ✓ nothing anywhere says the room is protected or covered
  ✓ the DEVICE_IN_SPACE edge carries an explicit non-coverage disclaimer
  ✓ every relationship repeats that it is factual only
  ✓ the four semantic distinctions are declared structurally
  ✓ and the compiled model carries them

== §5 — ABSENCE IS NOT A VIOLATION ==
  ✓ a building with no FLS data is NOT_DEFINED
  ✓ and has zero issues caused merely by absence
  ✓ no fire device was added automatically
  ✓ the status basis explains that only references exist
  ✓ a warehouse gets no sprinkler or hydrant just for being a warehouse
  ✓ a villa fixture without sprinklers reports zero, not a deficiency
  ✓ no issue code implies a missing element is a fault
  ✓ the spec states it plainly

== §6 — FIRE DOOR ONLY WHEN DECLARED ==
  ✓ the same architectural door yields no fire door without metadata
  ✓ the architectural door itself still exists untouched
  ✓ declaring it explicitly creates exactly one FLS reference
  ✓ the reference resolves to the real architectural opening
  ✓ its rating is carried, never inferred
  ✓ an unstated rating stays null with an explicit note
  ✓ the spec says a normal door is not a fire door

== §7 — BARRIER ONLY WHEN DECLARED ==
  ✓ the villa has real shared architectural walls
  ✓ but none of them is a fire barrier without metadata
  ✓ declaring one explicitly creates exactly one barrier referencing its host wall
  ✓ a structural wall is never promoted to a barrier either
  ✓ a barrier with no stated rating reports a data gap, not a violation
  ✓ the spec says an architectural wall is not a fire barrier

== §8 — STAIRS AND SHAFTS ARE NOT PROTECTED BY DEFAULT ==
  ✓ an adapted stair has protection_status unknown
  ✓ and it is never called a protected stair
  ✓ a declared protected stair says so explicitly
  ✓ a declared shaft protection is carried, never assumed
  ✓ an MEP riser is not a fire shaft by itself
  ✓ the audit counts only declared protected stairs
  ✓ the spec states the rule

== §9 — ZONES ARE NEVER INFERRED ==
  ✓ no zone exists without explicit data
  ✓ rooms are never turned into compartments
  ✓ a declared zone compiles and resolves its spaces
  ✓ it produces ZONE_CONTAINS_SPACE edges for exactly its declared spaces
  ✓ a zone with no spaces is reported as a data gap, not populated by inference
  ✓ the spec states the rule

== §10 — DETECTION, ALARM, SUPPRESSION, FIRE WATER ==
  ✓ devices map to declared categories
  ✓ a smoke detector is DETECTION and a sounder is ALARM
  ✓ a declared loop membership is represented, never designed
  ✓ a declared alarm zone is represented, never derived from floors
  ✓ a panel-controls-device edge exists only where declared
  ✓ sprinkler heads are represented with no spacing, coverage or K-factor
  ✓ an MEP sprinkler terminal is referenced rather than re-created
  ✓ a fire pump in MEP equipment is referenced as a FIRE_WATER device
  ✓ extinguishers and hose reels are represented without quantity or travel analysis

== §11 — SIGNAGE AND EMERGENCY LIGHTING ==
  ✓ an exit sign references a real exit
  ✓ SIGN_INDICATES_EXIT is emitted for it
  ✓ whether signage is required or adequate is never determined
  ✓ a sign pointing at a nonexistent exit is a model-integrity ERROR
  ✓ and the target is never invented
  ✓ emergency lights are represented with no lux or autonomy

== §12 — ASSEMBLY POINTS, REFUGE, SMOKE CONTROL ==
  ✓ an assembly point is represented at site scope
  ✓ no path from an exit to it is created
  ✓ an assembly point inside the footprint is reported as a data problem
  ✓ a refuge area exists only where declared
  ✓ a lobby, landing or corridor never becomes a refuge area
  ✓ accessibility is never evaluated for a refuge area
  ✓ smoke control entries are data placeholders only
  ✓ no smoke or airflow field is produced

== §13 — EGRESS, DISTANCE AND OCCUPANCY INTEGRATION ==
  ✓ a measured egress result can be quoted as factual data
  ✓ it is never compared to a code travel-distance limit
  ✓ no travel-distance limit exists anywhere in the layer
  ✓ a missing space yields no fabricated egress fact
  ✓ the building programme is never used as a fire occupancy classification
  ✓ the verified regulatory occupancy count is still zero

== §14 — MODEL INTEGRITY VALIDATION ==
  ✓ the deliberately broken fixture triggers every integrity check
  ✓ every issue code is declared in the spec with a severity
  ✓ issues are ordered ERROR first, then WARNING, then INFO
  ✓ no issue is a code or fire-compliance verdict
  ✓ an unknown FLS collection is reported and NOT interpreted
  ✓ a foreign building id is caught rather than silently re-namespaced
  ✓ a NaN coordinate is rejected rather than propagated
  ✓ a device located inside a stair void is reported as a fact, not a fault

== §15 — DETERMINISM, NAMESPACING AND TRANSFORMS ==
  ✓ compiling twice gives byte-identical output
  ✓ the compiler never mutates the model it reads
  ✓ a second building namespaces every FLS id
  ✓ two buildings can never collide on an id
  ✓ a transform never changes the compiled data
  ✓ the building transform is applied on read
  ✓ rotation is applied about the building origin

== §16 — REVISION HASH ==
  ✓ moving a detector changes the model hash
  ✓ removing a sprinkler changes the model hash
  ✓ changing a fire-door rating changes the model hash
  ✓ changing zone membership changes the model hash
  ✓ changing an exit-sign target changes the model hash
  ✓ changing a fire system reference changes the model hash
  ✓ toggling layer visibility does NOT change the model hash
  ✓ moving the camera still does not change the hash
  ✓ compiling the FLS model does not change the hash

== §17 — RENDER AND EXPORT ==
  ✓ render items use the FLS| naming convention
  ✓ every requested debug layer exists
  ✓ layer labels say data only, never compliance
  ✓ every render item declares its geometry is a display fallback
  ✓ render items never carry an engineering or compliance verdict
  ✓ colour marks the element type only, never a state
  ✓ no red-means-violation logic exists

== §18 — RULE ENGINE CONTRACT (INPUTS ONLY) ==
  ✓ device existence and counts are exposed as factual inputs
  ✓ an absent device type is exposed as false, not as a deficiency
  ✓ exit and zone counts are exposed
  ✓ fire-door and barrier ratings are exposed only when real
  ✓ no regulatory rule was added anywhere
  ✓ the rule inputs contain no threshold, limit or verdict

== §19 — NO ARCH / STRUCT / MEP / NAV / EGRESS / DISTANCE REGRESSION ==
  ✓ adding an FLS block changes no architectural element
  ✓ adding an FLS block changes no structural element
  ✓ adding an FLS block changes no MEP element
  ✓ compiling FLS does not mutate the MEP model
  ✓ relationships are identical with and without the FLS block
  ✓ navigation is identical with and without the FLS block
  ✓ egress selection and routing are identical
  ✓ walking distance is unchanged — no barrier or device reroutes anything
  ✓ and the model says so in writing

